---
// "Can I seed now?" Live answer from soil temperature, the calendar and the 7-day forecast. Logic in src/scripts/seedNow.js.
import PlaceChip from './PlaceChip.astro';
const { id = 'seed' } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="window tool sn" id={id} aria-labelledby={`${id}-h`} data-seed-now>
  <h2 id={`${id}-h`}>Can I Seed Now?</h2>
  <div class="soil-where sn-where"><span>Checking</span> <PlaceChip id={`${id}-place`} /></div>
  <p class="soil-note" data-sn-note hidden></p>
  <div class="mc-verdict sn-out" aria-live="polite">
    <span class="mc-word" data-tone="close" data-sn-word>CHECKING…</span>
    <p class="mc-line" data-sn-line>Looking at your soil and the forecast.</p>
    <p class="sn-rain" data-sn-rain></p>
  </div>
  <div class="mw-stats">
    <div><b data-sn-soil>–</b><span>Soil now</span></div>
    <div><b data-sn-next>–</b><span>Soil, next 7</span></div>
    <div><b data-sn-high>–</b><span>Highs, next 7</span></div>
    <div><b data-sn-rainv>–</b><span>Rain, next 7</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="sn-germ" data-sn-germ hidden>How long until you see green: perennial rye about 5 to 10 days, tall fescue 1 to 2 weeks, Kentucky bluegrass 2 to 4 weeks. Don’t panic in week one.</p>
  <p class="tool-fine">Grass seed sprouts best with soil between about 50 and 70°F. Around here the best window is September. Late August works in a cool year, and spring is a gamble. <a href="/resources/what-grass-seed-should-i-buy/">Which seed?</a> · <a href="/resources/lawn-care-order-of-operations/#ops-overseed">Seeding steps, in order</a></p>
</section>

<script>
  import { initSeedNow } from '../scripts/seedNow.js';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-seed-now]').forEach((el) => initSeedNow(el));
</script>
